"macOS draws a frame for every refresh: 30 Hz leaves the most of the emulated CPU to apps, at the cost of choppier animation; 60 Hz is smoother. Faster disk writes order them without waiting for a full sync; a sudden power loss could lose the last ones. Quicker wake keeps an idle CPU watching for work for 50 µs, at some battery cost. Superblocks let translated code run past conditional branches. Changes apply the next time a Mac starts." = "macOS 每次刷新都要画一帧：30 Hz 能把更多模拟 CPU 留给 App，代价是动画不够顺滑；60 Hz 更流畅。更快的磁盘写入会按顺序落盘而不用等待完全同步，突然断电可能丢掉最后几笔。更快唤醒让空闲 CPU 持续盯 50 微秒看有没有活干，会多耗一点电。超级块让翻译后的代码能跨越条件分支继续执行。改动会在下次启动 Mac 时生效。";
