"Every few minutes Henge checks its own memory, the running Mac's memory and its log, and trims the log when it grows too large. This keeps iOS from closing Henge on a phone with little memory. iOS decides when a backgrounded app may run, so the checks are exact while Henge is open and best-effort when it is not." = "Every few minutes Henge checks its own memory, the running Mac's memory and its log, and trims the log when it grows too large. This keeps iOS from closing Henge on a phone with little memory. iOS decides when a backgrounded app may run, so the checks are exact while Henge is open and best-effort when it is not.";
